(7490276, 1192237, 45631, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jomari:</b></div><hr/><i> I love this. It was in my top 3. Where exactly is it? Coolum? I have just returned home from a stay with my daughter and we visited that beautiful area, but I remember Coolum from years back because of these trees. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This is at Currimundi between Robe Street and Cockatoo Creek.  It''s a dog beach so gets a lot of use.</td>', 'Originally posted by jomari: I love this. It was in my top 3. Where exactly is it? Coolum? I have just returned home from a stay with my daughter and we visited that beautiful area, but I remember Coolum from years back because of these trees.   This is at Currimundi between Robe Street and Cockatoo Creek.  It''s a dog beach so gets a lot of use.', '2017-01-03 04:30:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(7490325, 1192427, 138630, '<td valign="top">I like this best, too, though I could have used a little perspective correction.  The leaning street light (esp) and the bit of white in the upper right both bothered me - pulling the upper corners out just a bit would have helped.  But I loved the inclusion of the runners.</td>', 'I like this best, too, though I could have used a little perspective correction.  The leaning street light (esp) and the bit of white in the upper right both bothered me - pulling the upper corners out just a bit would have helped.  But I loved the inclusion of the runners.', '2017-01-03 13:40:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(7490327, 1192121, 50695, '<td valign="top">this harkens back to the first landscapes. a lone figure eclipsed by the majesty of nature.</td>', 'this harkens back to the first landscapes. a lone figure eclipsed by the majesty of nature.', '2017-01-03 14:01:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(7490328, 1192442, 50695, '<td valign="top">sorry I didn''t get back to this. It would have ribboned in my head.</td>', 'sorry I didn''t get back to this. It would have ribboned in my head.', '2017-01-03 14:03:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(7490329, 1192394, 50695, '<td valign="top">I like the composition. It is peaceful. This was in my top 5. and for the second challenge in a row, I was your top score.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2017-01-03 14:04:36.</i></td>', 'I like the composition. It is peaceful. This was in my top 5. and for the second challenge in a row, I was your top score.', '2017-01-03 14:04:16.000000', '2017-01-03 14:04:36.000000', 0),
(7490330, 1192426, 50695, '<td valign="top">I like this a lot, with the hints of composition behind the foreground explosion</td>', 'I like this a lot, with the hints of composition behind the foreground explosion', '2017-01-03 14:05:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(7490332, 1191914, 50695, '<td valign="top">I love the chalky highlights, well composed.</td>', 'I love the chalky highlights, well composed.', '2017-01-03 14:08:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(7490333, 1192456, 50695, '<td valign="top">I like the energy and composition. I gave this a 7 and then I lost the challenge somewhere and stopped voting.</td>', 'I like the energy and composition. I gave this a 7 and then I lost the challenge somewhere and stopped voting.', '2017-01-03 14:09:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7490336, 1192351, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that contributes well to the challenge<br/> <br/>This is a lovely night scene that is enhanced by good mono processing. Whilst the lights are understandably blown the exposure overall is good, there is good detail throughout. Unlike your commenters, I would actually like to see more foreground but it would need to be sharply in focus too. By cropping the tops of the tall trees it would move it all to the upper third and create a more interesting composition but as I said before this would only work with a larger DOF with light playing on the focussed shapes and shades on the water.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that contributes well to the challenge This is a lovely night scene that is enhanced by good mono processing. Whilst the lights are understandably blown the exposure overall is good, there is good detail throughout. Unlike your commenters, I would actually like to see more foreground but it would need to be sharply in focus too. By cropping the tops of the tall trees it would move it all to the upper third and create a more interesting composition but as I said before this would only work with a larger DOF with light playing on the focussed shapes and shades on the water.', '2017-01-03 14:28:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(7490337, 1192418, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that contributes well to the challenge<br/> <br/>Well, I think Glad2badad has done an excellent critique already and very succinctly summed up everything I want to say about your image, I will try to add a little further detail. The background does not add to the overall result a clean white background would greatly simplify and add impact. Because cameras are geared to give average results for average scenes they will always underexpose a predominantly white scene such as snow so you always need to give 1 or 2 stops +EC in order to get nice crisp whites. The white balance is in need of a slightly warmer shift to reduce the blueness overall. Happy New Year and good luck in the coming year Marcel.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that contributes well to the challenge Well, I think Glad2badad has done an excellent critique already and very succinctly summed up everything I want to say about your image, I will try to add a little further detail. The background does not add to the overall result a clean white background would greatly simplify and add impact. Because cameras are geared to give average results for average scenes they will always underexpose a predominantly white scene such as snow so you always need to give 1 or 2 stops +EC in order to get nice crisp whites. The white balance is in need of a slightly warmer shift to reduce the blueness overall. Happy New Year and good luck in the coming year Marcel.', '2017-01-03 14:39:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(7490341, 1192427, 97225, '<td valign="top">I, too, like this one best. The perspective doesn''t bother me. I think the slight leaning in of the outer trees contributes to the mood.</td>', 'I, too, like this one best. The perspective doesn''t bother me. I think the slight leaning in of the outer trees contributes to the mood.', '2017-01-03 16:04:30.000000', NULL, 0),
